# Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Houses of Hermes: Societates — House Jerbiton (Lore)

**Version:** 0.5.1
**Source:** Houses of Hermes: Societates (Atlas Games) — Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Chapter Two (pp. 39–70)
**Publisher:** Atlas Games

> Chapter Two’s narrative, verbatim: House Jerbiton’s history from Flavius to the fall of
> Constantinople, what living tastefully means to its magi, the little structure the House has,
> and its leagues. The chapter’s mechanics are structured records elsewhere — urban magic, the
> creation of beautiful things, perception and deception, and memory in `armdef-houses-societates-0.5-jerbiton.ttrpg`;
> the new Virtues and Flaws in `armdef-houses-societates-0.5-jerbiton-virtues-flaws.ttrpg`; the sidebars as GUIDANCE and
> TABLE records in `armdef-houses-societates-0.5-jerbiton-sidebars.ttrpg`. The House itself is the canonical
> `^"House Jerbiton"` DEF in `armdef-0.5-houses.ttrpg`.

